{
 "text": " something strange: the shadow of the tree seemed to move faster than the sun itself.\n\nElena was puzzled. She ran to the village elder, Mr. Thorne, who was known for his wisdom and love of riddles. \u201cMr. Thorne,\u201d she asked, \u201cwhy does the shadow move so quickly?\u201d\n\nMr. Thorne smiled and said, \u201cAh, Elena, shadows are like time itself\u2014they move faster when the light changes quickly. But tell me, what do you think causes the sun to rise?\u201d\n\nElena thought for a moment. \u201cI think it\u2019s because the earth turns, right?\u201d\n\n\u201cExactly!\u201d Mr. Thorne exclaimed. \u201cAnd now, let\u2019s solve a riddle together. If the earth rotates once every 24 hours, how many times does it rotate in a week?\u201d\n\nElena counted on her fingers. \u201cSeven days, so seven times?\u201d\n\n\u201cNot quite,\u201d Mr. Thorne chuckled. \u201cThink about it\u2014how many hours are in a day?\u201d\n\n\u201cTwenty-four,\u201d Elena replied.\n\n\u201cRight! So, how many hours are in a week?\u201d\n\n\u201cSeventy-two,\u201d Elena said confidently.\n\n\u201cCorrect! Now, if the earth rotates once every ",
